{"event":"intent","sources":["f002","f001","origin"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=hci-completed-length-trust; Search only snapshots/s03. Genuinely new mechanism branch surfaced by fact f002, distinct from parse-time wire counts, allocation arithmetic, error-unwind poisoning, and parsed protocol reply fields: controller- or device-completed transfer metadata — urb->actual_length and analogues such as request actual/residual counts set by hardware or device firmware at completion time — consumed by completion handlers as a copy length or iteration bound without cross-check against the locally requested size such as transfer_buffer_length. Primary target flagged unresolved by f002: drivers/greybus/es2.c near line 844, where greybus_data_rcvd(hd, cport_id, urb->transfer_buffer, urb->actual_length) hands the HCI-set length into gb_connection_recv/gb_connection_recv_request whose memcpy(message->buffer, data, size) destination is sized from local request state — determine whether actual_length is bounded anywhere between bulk-in URB completion and the copy, and whether an oversized or malicious device reply drives an OOB read or write. Then sweep the other URB/request completion handlers in this one snapshot that use actual_length/actual/resid fields as copy or loop lengths. For each candidate record file:line of the completion callback, the metadata field, the missing bound check, and the consuming copy/loop; a negative result must cite the completion handlers examined. The seed usbip path itself is demonstration-only and must never be reported as the finding. Save a structured artifact (execution_status, candidates or evidence-backed negative) for snapshots/s03 only."}
